  "note": "The paper bankroll went through zero on 2026-09-03. The pre-registered rule sizes every ticket at up to 5% of bankroll and a prop slate offers hundreds of them at once, so the tickets in this ledger stake 19,651 units against a 1,000-unit bankroll \u2014 19.7x exposure in a single evening. Emission stops at ruin because a non-positive bankroll has no Kelly stake. Nothing was re-tuned after seeing this: the per-ticket cap and the 1,000-ticket Stage 1 gate in docs/bankroll.md are not compatible on this book, and that is a question for the pre-registration, not for the code. That question was answered on 2026-09-09 by Amendment 1: the total stake across one slate is capped at 20% of bankroll, the sizing changes and nothing else does, the Stage 1 window restarts at the amendment, and these tickets stay in the ledger flagged `stage0` without counting toward the gate."
